{"name":"Blue Bayou","hex":"#bec4d3","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"},{"term":"bayou","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A slow-moving, often stagnant creek or river.","A swamp; a marshy (stagnant) body of water."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bayou"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blue Bayou","blocks":[{"text":"\"Blue Bayou\" is a song written by Roy Orbison and Joe Melson. It was originally sung and recorded by Orbison, who had an international hit with his version in 1963. It later became Linda Ronstadt's signature song, with which she scored a top 5 hit with her cover in 1977. Many others have since recorded the song."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Blue_bayou_roy_orbison_US_original_single.webp/330px-Blue_bayou_roy_orbison_US_original_single.webp?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Bayou","wikidata":"Q4928860"},{"title":"Blue Bayou (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Blue Bayou is a 2021 American drama film written and directed by Justin Chon. The film stars Chon, Alicia Vikander, Mark O'Brien, Linh Dan Pham, Sydney Kowalske, Vondie Curtis-Hall, and Emory Cohen."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/6d/Blue_Bayou_%28film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Bayou_(film)","wikidata":"Q84010895"},{"title":"Bayou","blocks":[{"text":"In usage in the Southern United States, a bayou is a body of water typically found in a flat, low-lying area. It may refer to an extremely slow-moving stream, marshy lake, or wetland. They typically contain brackish water highly conducive to fish life and plankton. Bayous are commonly found in the Gulf Coast region of the southern United States, especially in the Mississippi River Delta, though they also exist elsewhere."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Atchafalaya_Basin.jpg/330px-Atchafalaya_Basin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bayou","wikidata":"Q812585"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Roy_Orbison_in_1965.jpg/500px-Roy_Orbison_in_1965.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Roy_Orbison_in_1965.jpg/500px-Roy_Orbison_in_1965.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Roy Orbison, 1965","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARoy_Orbison_in_1965.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/75/Blue_bayou_linda_ronstadt_US_single_side-A.webp/250px-Blue_bayou_linda_ronstadt_US_single_side-A.webp?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/75/Blue_bayou_linda_ronstadt_US_single_side-A.webp?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/75/Blue_bayou_linda_ronstadt_US_single_side-A.webp/250px-Blue_bayou_linda_ronstadt_US_single_side-A.webp?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlue_bayou_linda_ronstadt_US_single_side-A.webp"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Linda_Ronstadt_1976.jpg/500px-Linda_Ronstadt_1976.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Linda_Ronstadt_1976.jpg/1280px-Linda_Ronstadt_1976.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Linda_Ronstadt_1976.jpg/500px-Linda_Ronstadt_1976.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Linda Ronstadt, 1976","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALinda_Ronstadt_1976.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/2010._%D0%94%D0%BE%D0%BD%D0%B5%D1%86%D0%BA._%D0%9A%D0%B0%D1%80%D0%BD%D0%B0%D0%B2%D0%B0%D0%BB_%D0%BD%D0%B0_%D0%B4%D0%B5%D0%BD%D1%8C_%D0%B3%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%B4%D0%B0_010.jpg/500px-2010._%D0%94%D0%BE%D0%BD%D0%B5%D1%86%D0%BA._%D0%9A%D0%B0%D1%80%D0%BD%D0%B0%D0%B2%D0%B0%D0%BB_%D0%BD%D0%B0_%D0%B4%D0%B5%D0%BD%D1%8C_%D0%B3%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%B4%D0%B0_010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wi